{{Quote|Remember, the Imperial fuel depot is our primary target.|Hera Syndulla, to the pilots of Phoenix Squadron|<ref name="Rebel Assault" />}}
The '''Lothal City fuel depot''',<ref name="Jedi Night EG">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/jedi-night-episode-guide|text="Jedi Night" Episode Guide &#124; Star Wars Rebels}}</ref> also known simply as the '''Lothal fuel depot''',<ref name="Fuel DB">{{Databank|lothal-fuel-depot|Lothal fuel depot}}</ref> was a fueling facility located in [[Capital City]] on the [[planet]] [[Lothal]]. During the [[Lothal campaign]], the facility was the primary target of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance's]] [[ Phoenix Squadron]] when they [[Attack on Lothal|attacked Lothal]]. After the battle, the fuel depot was unscathed, and the entire [[squadron]] was shot down, leading to the capture of rebel leader [[Hera Syndulla]].<ref name="Rebel Assault" /> When [[Kanan Jarrus]] mounted a [[Rescue of Hera Syndulla (Lothal)|mission to rescue Syndulla]], he freed her and fled to the fuel depot to rendezvous with the rebels and escape. However, the facility was destroyed by the [[Galactic Empire|Empire]] on the orders of [[Governor]] [[Arihnda Pryce]], who saw the prospect of [[Death|killing]] the [[Jedi Knight]] too good to pass up. Although Jarrus perished, he successfully rescued Syndulla.<ref name="Jedi Night">{{Rebels|Jedi Night}}</ref> Following the destruction of the depot, [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]] informed Pryce of his irritation about its destruction and consequences for his [[TIE/d "Defender" Multi-Role Starfighter|TIE Defender project]], saying that she acted irresponsibly and that he would deal with her when he arrived on Lothal from [[Coruscant]].<ref name="DUME">{{Rebels|DUME}}</ref>

